---

CastGood's own source is MIT. The installer additionally redistributes third-party
software under its own terms — most importantly ffmpeg, which is GPL-3.0-or-later,
and is not covered by the licence above.

ffmpeg is invoked as a separate program over a command-line boundary, never linked
and never through FFI (docs/DECISIONS.md, 2026-08-13). That arm's-length arrangement
is what lets CastGood's own source carry a permissive licence while the installer
ships a GPL binary beside it.

The installed application carries, next to the executable:

  resources/bin/LICENSE.ffmpeg.txt   ffmpeg's GPL-3.0 text
  resources/bin/BUILD.ffmpeg.txt     the exact configuration it was built with
  resources/bin/ffmpeg-build.json    version, builder, and the upstream commit
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt            every bundled npm package and its licence

The corresponding source for the bundled ffmpeg is the upstream commit named in
`ffmpeg-build.json`, and the build is published unmodified by https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/.
